  "dom_id": "step-q180750",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA={{n}^{4}:n\\in Z}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $A?$",
  "worked_solution": "The elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={n}^{4},\\,n\\in Z={0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down some terms of our sequence until the pattern becomes clear.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \u22ee \\\\ {a}_{-3} & =(-3)^{4}=81 \\\\ {a}_{-2} & =(-2)^{4}=16 \\\\ {a}_{-1} & =(-1)^{4}=1 \\\\ {a}_{0} & ={0}^{4}=0 \\\\ {a}_{1} & ={1}^{4}=1 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={2}^{4}=16 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={3}^{4}=81 \\\\  & \u22ee\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set consists of the elements\n\n$$\nA={0,1,16,81\u2026}.\n$$\n\nThese are just the fourth powers including $0.$ Continuing the pattern, we have\n\n$$\nA={0,1,16,81,256,625,\u2026}.\n$$",
